Stop two PHP warnings per empty field, per row, on every order lines screen.

getFieldValue() reads the first value of a field without checking that there is
one:

  $data = $entity->get($field)->getValue()[0]['value'];

When a line has no quantity yet, getValue() answers an empty array, so [0] is
undefined and ['value'] is then read off NULL. That is two warnings for every
empty field of every row:

  Warning: Undefined array key 0 in
  Drupal\views_simple_math_field\Plugin\views\field\SimpleMathField::getFieldValue()
  Warning: Trying to access array offset on null

On this site that is fifteen warnings on a single load of the editable order
lines table, and a new order starts with every quantity empty. Nothing breaks,
the page answers 200, but the log is where real failures are looked for and this
buries them.

$data ends up being NULL with or without the fix, so the calculation behaves
exactly as before. The only thing that changes is the noise.

diff --git a/src/Plugin/views/field/SimpleMathField.php b/src/Plugin/views/field/SimpleMathField.php
--- a/src/Plugin/views/field/SimpleMathField.php
+++ b/src/Plugin/views/field/SimpleMathField.php
@@ -343,7 +343,10 @@ protected function getFieldValue(ResultRow $values, $entity, $field) {
         }
       }
       else {
-        $data = $entity->get($field)->getValue()[0]['value'];
+        // An empty field answers an empty array, so reading [0]['value'] off it
+        // leaves two warnings in the log per field and per row. The result is
+        // NULL either way, which is what the calculation already handled.
+        $data = $entity->get($field)->getValue()[0]['value'] ?? NULL;
       }
 
       return $data;
